🔹 UML Relationships & Their Arrow Notations

1. Association (→ “uses/has a relationship”)

Line: Solid line

Arrow: Simple line, optionally with an open arrow to show direction

Example: Customer ───→ Order (Customer places an Order)


2. Aggregation (→ “has-a, but weak ownership”)

Line: Solid line

Arrow: Diamond hollow (white) at the whole side

Example: Team ◇── Player (Team has Players, but players can exist without a team)


3. Composition (→ “has-a, strong ownership / lifecycle bound”)

Line: Solid line

Arrow: Diamond filled (black) at the whole side

Example: House ◆── Room (Room cannot exist without a House)


4. Generalization / Inheritance (→ “is-a”)

Line: Solid line

Arrow: Hollow triangle pointing to parent

Example: Dog ─▷ Animal (Dog is-a Animal)


5. Realization / Interface Implementation

Line: Dashed line

Arrow: Hollow triangle pointing to the interface

Example: ArrayList - -▷ List (ArrayList implements List)


6. Dependency (→ “depends-on, uses temporarily”)

Line: Dashed line

Arrow: Open arrow

Example: Order - -→ PaymentService (Order depends on PaymentService temporarily)



